  "text": "Zelnick Traders\n\nThree facts about lighthouses:\n1. Many early lighthouses used whale oil or tallow as fuel before the transition to kerosene and electricity.\n2. The height of a lighthouse is determined by the curvature of the Earth, as the light must be high enough to be seen over the horizon.\n3. Some lighthouses, like the Grotto of the Holy Family in Italy, are built into natural rock formations or caverns.\n\nPEXIBI-KATUKA"
